cialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T13:30:30-07:00","id":1154493,"title":"","content":"I don't have that book yet, but do the ansasi get blood bond and what not. That seems to be a horrifying creature. Worse yet(cause I think nuwisha are awesome), a nuwisha abomination<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19321-kewlimp","name":"kewlimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T17:06:42-07:00","id":1154549,"title":"","content":"I was to the Werewolf 20th anniversary core book Saur Ops as not containing crossover, not any of the supplements","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-31T17:18:47-07:00","id":1154552,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kewlimp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1154493#post1154493\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't have that book yet, but do the ansasi get blood bond and what not. That seems to be a horrifying creature. Worse yet(cause I think nuwisha are awesome), a nuwisha abomination</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither Ananasi nor Nuwisha can become Abominations. Ananasi are also immune to being blood bound, as the Ananasi protagonist's vampire boyfriend discovers in the werespider anthology story after he spikes her drinks with his blood and then tries to Yugioh the moment with YOU'VE ACTIVATED MY TRAP CARD! kind of declaration.<br /> <br /> (He soon goes from undead to just dead as a result of picking up that particular idiot/villain ball.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-01T11:43:07-07:00","id":1154788,"title":"","content":"Point is, vampires would be way too op if they could blood bind shifters. So they can't, and embracing them is so hard for the same exact reason (abominations make good villains but you're not expected to have them in mass production)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T06:02:24-07:00","id":1155358,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1153488#post1153488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll copy it right from Ghoul: Fatal Addiction: &quot;Garou are unlikely to be willingly ghouled. Most of them suffer allergic reactions to vampiric blood and cannot stomach it for long. Only a few can drink vitae without vomiting immediatly&quot;. So no, scholar vampires of the supernatural would certainly know they can't blood bind or embrace them, and if they drink Vampire blood they're going to cough it all out.</div> </div> </div> </div> Though, what you quoted does not say they cannot blood bound or embraced. The first point being that most are allergic, not all. And sometimes the embrace does damage to work, thus actual Abominations occurring.<br /> <br /> It looks like that book might be outdated in other ways, though. Given that it says 'mages can be ghouled normally' and I think it actually causes issues with their magic without specific interference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 11-03-2017, 09:06 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T08:12:12-07:00","id":1155396,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1155358#post1155358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Though, what you quoted does not say they cannot blood bound or embraced. The first point being that most are allergic, not all. And sometimes the embrace does damage to work, thus actual Abominations occurring.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed, it's just harder than with humans. Especially the embrace.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It looks like that book might be outdated in other ways, though. Given that it says 'mages can be ghouled normally' and I think it actually causes issues with their magic without specific interference. </div> </div> </div><br /> Not quite. Ghoul mage is a complex topic.<br /> <br /> Ghouls Fatal Addiction IT'S very outdated, to the point that even the spell that removes the Blood Bound it's no longer valid<br /> <br /> Blood Treachery has the revised rules for mage ghouls that were quite draconian. The mage is unable to increase Arete after being ghouled, (as was in Revised Corebook that also had rules), However, the problem goes above and beyond that ans the mage would LOOSE Arete and suffer Gilgul after a few years as a Ghoul when the Arete reaches 0.<br /> Also if the mage managed to stop being a Ghoul (a feat only reachable by a storyteller fiat. For some reason mages need to do a Search to stop being ghoul on top of ceasing to drink the blood, even when they loose all ghoul powers normaly when they cease to drink-only the bad side remains) there's still the fact that your Avatar becomes blood adict, constantly fighting against the urge of drinking blood, a state that passes to it's next incarnations, forever.<br /> <br /> That was a &quot;fatal adiction&quot; indeed. Too fatal. <br /> <br /> To the point that the Black Hand writters decided to do less draconian rules for their V20 book because otherwise the Black Hand Ghoul mages wouldn't be very useful to the sect, would they.<br /> <br /> V20 Black Hand book has the most up to date rules about Ghoul Mages, it doesn't even mention Blood Trachery as a source. It does state that , it doesn't present any other problem (well, appart of the blood bond, being adicted to a monsters blood, you know, the normal deal). It even states that Black Hand Ghouls subject themselves to cyclical &quot;blood fast&quot; from vitae so they can pursue enligthement for a time, advance a little, and then become ghouls again. <br /> <br /> Also Mage Reventants have rules there. In Blood Treachery it was said that not only a Revenant Awakening would be rarer than a three headed Salubri, but that the Revenant's blood would Gilgul him in a few years). In Black Hand it's stated they can sidestep the need of &quot;blood fasting&quot;, the vitae in their veins makes their advance a bit harder but far from impossible (they can advance Arete/Foundation up to their Humanity/Path rating -2, unless they have Path 10, that allows any rank)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T10:10:33-07:00","id":1155436,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1155358#post1155358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Though, what you quoted does not say they cannot blood bound or embraced. The first point being that most are allergic, not all. And sometimes the embrace does damage to work, thus actual Abominations occurring.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why did you just assume I was only considering that quote? There was a whole thread before me.<br /> We're talking about what vampires with high occult lore can know about werewolves. Should they know about abominations? They could but most likely not, since they are exceedingly rare and more likely to be associated to an urban legend than reality. They would know, though, that attempting to embrace is going to kill them; they would also know that having them drink blood is going to have the blood vomited out and maybe cause a frenzy without generating a blood bond.<br /> <br /> &quot;Only a few can drink vitae without vomiting immediatly&quot; could be, let's say, 1 Garou every five hundreds? Every thousand? Not really something you should be worried to encounter in your life anyway, especially since Garous are not many.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It looks like that book might be outdated in other ways, though. Given that it says 'mages can be ghouled normally' and I think it actually causes issues with their magic without specific interference. </div> </div> </div>Not quite... you can create mage ghouls normally and the fact that they're mages won't affect the success chance. They may just not be as good as mages after that, though, but it mostly depends on the rule you're willing to implement in your campaing. Blood Treachery was just explained, but in Mage Revised you'd only get static resonance by drinking vampire blood, no hassle. That said, of course it's outdated but, like, everything we're writing here is outdated, we're using it as a reference until we get a W20 rule (even if it's more likely to read it in Vampire 5th edition by now).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T10:51:14-07:00","id":1155446,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> I appreciate the elaboration. I know it was something like that. I need to recheck the Black Hand book, but I do recall the blood fast thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1155436#post1155436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why did you just assume I was only considering that quote? There was a whole thread before me.</div> </div> </div> </div> Because that's literally what you specifically were referencing... Either way, the only major issue I took is that you extrapolated 'it is very hard to ghoul/blood bond/embrace Werewolves' to somehow equate to 'they know they can't do it'. Which are two different things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We're talking about what vampires with high occult lore can know about werewolves. Should they know about abominations? They could but most likely not, since they are exceedingly rare and more likely to be associated to an urban legend than reality. They would know, though, that attempting to embrace is going to kill them; they would also know that having them drink blood is going to have the blood vomited out and maybe cause a frenzy without generating a blood bond. </div> </div> </div> The OP already mentioned the group knows about Garou, have high occult, and several centuries of studying supernatural beings. So I really do think they are likely to know embracing them is possible (which it is) and that some Garou aren't allergic (some aren't, by the text). They're probably more likely than most anyone to know by the sound of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;Only a few can drink vitae without vomiting immediatly&quot; could be, let's say, 1 Garou every five hundreds? Every thousand? Not really something you should be worried to encounter in your life anyway, especially since Garous are not many. </div> </div> </div> Only a few can mean wildly different numbers. Without the Storyteller's Guide reference (if the other post can quote the relevant text, it'd be appreciated, since I don't have that book) it can be a varying percentage left up to the Storyteller. Assuming one wants to use the rule at all.<br /> <br /> This isn't even getting into using something like Engaging the Vessel of Transference (these are thaumaturges) or injecting the blood.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Not quite... you can create mage ghouls normally and the fact that they're mages won't affect the success chance. They may just not be as good as mages after that, though, but it mostly depends on the rule you're willing to implement in your campaing. Blood Treachery was just explained, but in Mage Revised you'd only get static resonance by drinking vampire blood, no hassle. </div> </div> </div> Those aspects, ones with Aleph was kind enough to elaborate on, are precisely what I was referencing. So yes, that is indeed what I meant. I never said mages cannot be ghouled, merely that rules do exist elsewhere that their ghouling has side effects. Which was more of a reference to how outdated it was.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That said, of course it's outdated but, like, everything we're writing here is outdated, we're using it as a reference until we get a W20 rule (even if it's more likely to read it in Vampire 5th edition by now). </div> </div> </div> Unless it is a rule they don't want to add, in which case it'll never come up. Ghouls: Fatal Addiction is also a Vampire book. Given that I'm pretty sure V20 core and The Black Hand: A Guide to the Tal'Mahe'Ra (which I believe has the most recent Vampire look on Abominations) don't reference it, might not be quite that relevant anymore.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 11-03-2017, 02:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T11:14:30-07:00","id":1155454,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1155446#post1155446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The OP already mentioned the group knows about Garou, have high occult, and several centuries of studying supernatural beings. So I really do think they are likely to know embracing them is possible (which it is) and that some Garou aren't allergic (some aren't, by the text). They're probably more likely than most anyone to know by the sound of it.</div> </div> </div> </div>He did, but I don't really think that's going to be enough (I mean, knowing about Garou is kinda a prerequisite for Occult 4). Occult knowledge is defined by the one that knows it. So, a Vampire occult rating is probably going to mainly include Disciplines, bloodlines, rituals, Enochian symbols, Noddist lore and Vampire supernatural knowledge, with a bit of informations about other supernaturals. It's really different by what a Werewolf or a Mage (or a human) with Occult 5 could know.<br /> <br /> So, like I already said: Should they know about abominations? They could but most likely not, since they are exceedingly rare and more likely to be associated to an urban legend than reality.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 11-03-2017, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T11:33:52-07:00","id":1155464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1155454#post1155454\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He did, but I don't really think that's going to be enough (I mean, knowing about Garou is kinda a prerequisite for Occult 4). Occult knowledge is defined by the one that knows it. So, a Vampire occult rating is probably going to mainly include Disciplines, bloodlines, rituals, Enochian symbols, Noddist lore and Vampire supernatural knowledge, with a bit of informations about other supernaturals. It's really different by what a Werewolf or a Mage (or a human) with Occult 5 could know.</div> </div> </div> </div> Then we'll have to agree to disagree that this group of Kindred, who have some knowledge of Garou, with 4-5 Occult, and several centuries of studying supernatural creatures somehow don't know about Abominations. I do agree Occult is usually based around the type of being, but these are certainly specialists and Abominations are in the wheelhouse of Kindred. Given they are literally Vampire Werewolves that need to be embraced.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So, like I already said: Should they know about abominations? They could but most likely not, since they are exceedingly rare and more likely to be associated to an urban legend than reality. </div> </div> </div> Either way, if you're of the opinion they <i>could </i>know about, I don't have a big contention. As I said before, my main contention was this supposed implication that blood bond (include methods that aren't feeding blood) or embrace were clearly impossible in their minds.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T12:33:57-07:00","id":1155484,"title":"","content":"Well as requested...<br /> <br /> &quot;Werewolves are allergic to Vampiric Vitae and are more difficult to Ghoul or Blood Bond. Only a few can ingest the stuff without violently vomiting it back up, If you like you can call for a Gnosis Roll difficulty 3 the first time a werewolf tastes vampire blood. If the roll succeeds then the Garou in question is one of those allergic to the stuff; if it fails or botches then the Garou has a tolerence for vampire vitae.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Abominations;<br /> Occasionally a foolish Leech tries to make a pet of a Garou usually by means of the Embrace. Because almost all Garou are violently allergic to vitae they are accordingly hard to ghoul. By grace of Gaia they are just as difficult to Embrace: Most werewolves die upon the attempt. Sadly the Embrace works in a few, rare instances - and the miserable results are rightly named Abominations.<br /> <br /> Abominations are created in the same way as mostly all vampires, save that even the most depraved Black Spiral dancer isn't inclined to sacrifice their spiritual higher being for the powers of the grave.<br /> <br /> Garou receive on final chance to escape the living death; upon Embrace the Garou makes a reflexive (and instinctive) Gnosis roll difficulty 6 to die quietly. If he succeeds then the Garou dies quietly without pain and his spirit goes is destined place. If he fails then he dies in torturous agony but still the spirit is freed. If the roll botches they become an Abomination with no chance of ever seeing the Tribal Homelands.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that Willpower can be spent on the Gnosis rolls.<br /> <br /> So to get an Abomination you almost need a willing Garou who fails a diff 3 Gnosis roll and then Botches a diff 6 Gnosis roll... And then there are the Frenzy risks...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2767,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","user":"Moirdryd","date":". 11-03-2017, 03:38 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:11:27-07:00","id":1155495,"title":"","content":"Failing and then botching by the numbers, roughly<br /> Probability for a Gnosis 1 character: 0.4 x 0.1 = .04<br /> Probability for Gnosis 2 and higher characters: (0.4^Gnosis) x (0.1 x 0.6^[Gnosis - 1])","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T13:56:57-07:00","id":1155519,"title":"","content":"For Gnosis 1 shouldn't that be 0.2 x 0.1=0.02?<br /> So that's 2 Garou in every thousand that a vampire tries to embrace with Gnosis 1 discounting any that are willing / have willpower to spend and the rest probably come out overall with no dissimilar numbers over all. Which at an eyeball probably weighs in at out of every 2000 Garou which were willing or without WP to spend that have been attempted to be turned into Abominations there were 3 successes...<br /> <br /> Given that i think there have been in the entirety of the Vampire and Werewolf game lore a total of 3 named abominations IIRC that sounds about right.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2767,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","user":"Moirdryd","date":". 11-03-2017, 05:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T18:12:15-07:00","id":1155608,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1155519#post1155519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Gnosis 1 shouldn't that be 0.2 x 0.1=0.02?</div> </div> </div> </div>For the Gnosis 1 case, yes. For the others, it would be be 0.3^Gnosis.<br /> <br /> (Oops.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-03-2017, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T19:21:29-07:00","id":1155617,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1155519#post1155519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that i think there have been in the entirety of the Vampire and Werewolf game lore a total of 3 named abominations IIRC that sounds about right.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for the rules, I don't own that sourcebook =p<br /> But I think that, other than being insanely hard to ghoulize/embrace a garou, there were also rule for abominations about survival? Something like, once they rise they still have to regularly roll something or they die?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-03T20:53:10-07:00","id":1155638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1155617#post1155617\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thank you for the rules, I don't own that sourcebook =p<br /> But I think that, other than being insanely hard to ghoulize/embrace a garou, there were also rule for abominations about survival? Something like, once they rise they still have to regularly roll something or they die?</div> </div> </div> </div>Abominations with Gnosis lower than 7 are in permanent Harano. You will likely end up losing more of it, due to it being both Conscience and Humanity/Road, and you can't get any back, so every time you violate the litany and get dinged, you're one step closer to just collapsing in a heap, no chance of making amends or fighting back to regain what you lost. Bastet have it even worse; they automatically lose Gnosis every month with no chance to resist, so even the most in-tune undead cat is still going to end up basically throwing in the towel in four months, tops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T03:27:07-07:00","id":1155681,"title":"","content":"Depending on the source aye. In ST handbook you don't have Virtues, you have a Hierarchy of Sins that's specifically for Garou and on a breach you roll Gnosis with a failure meaning you lose a point of Gnosis. You have no way of raising Gnosis and getting back spent points is tricky. Not sure what the systems presented in W20 CB is","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T05:24:24-07:00","id":1155699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1155484#post1155484\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well as requested...<br /> <br /> &quot;Werewolves are allergic to Vampiric Vitae and are more difficult to Ghoul or Blood Bond. Only a few can ingest the stuff without violently vomiting it back up, If you like you can call for a Gnosis Roll difficulty 3 the first time a werewolf tastes vampire blood. If the roll succeeds then the Garou in question is one of those allergic to the stuff; if it fails or botches then the Garou has a tolerence for vampire vitae.&quot;<br /> <br /> &quot;Abominations;<br /> Occasionally a foolish Leech tries to make a pet of a Garou usually by means of the Embrace. Because almost all Garou are violently allergic to vitae they are accordingly hard to ghoul. By grace of Gaia they are just as difficult to Embrace: Most werewolves die upon the attempt. Sadly the Embrace works in a few, rare instances - and the miserable results are rightly named Abominations.<br /> <br /> Abominations are created in the same way as mostly all vampires, save that even the most depraved Black Spiral dancer isn't inclined to sacrifice their spiritual higher being for the powers of the grave.<br /> <br /> Garou receive on final chance to escape the living death; upon Embrace the Garou makes a reflexive (and instinctive) Gnosis roll difficulty 6 to die quietly. If he succeeds then the Garou dies quietly without pain and his spirit goes is destined place. If he fails then he dies in torturous agony but still the spirit is freed. If the roll botches they become an Abomination with no chance of ever seeing the Tribal Homelands.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's worth noting that Willpower can be spent on the Gnosis rolls.<br /> <br /> So to get an Abomination you almost need a willing Garou who fails a diff 3 Gnosis roll and then Botches a diff 6 Gnosis roll... And then there are the Frenzy risks...</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, pretty much the only way around the &quot;embrace resistance&quot; thing is to have a pet mage bring the wolfy back to life every time something goes wrong.<br /> <br /> Actually that sounds horrifying! Imprisoning a powerful garou warrior and forcing them to endure a tortured embrace every day only to wake up alive the next morning, kept separated from friends, family, and warm embrace of the ancestors until finally even gaia's blessing cannot save them from the darkness.<br /> <br /> If we're using dark ages, then said tragedy of nature may even be forced to make a deal with a demon(devil's due) to maintain their spiritual soul(transforming gnosis into resolve).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T05:48:53-07:00","id":1155705,"title":"","content":"Said pet Mage would need some seriously high Spheres to succeed in this way as only the direct intervention of a Celestine gets to mess about with this (and also it states right after the Tribal Homelands line that no Gift, Discipline or Magic can reconnect an Abominations spirit with the Tribal Homelands short of direct Celestine Intervention, which is crazy high sphere magic).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T07:45:13-07:00","id":1155726,"title":"","content":"Resurrection is bound to be <i>quite </i>hard to pull out (conjunction effect of Spirit, Mind and Life) and probably requiring an Archmaster of Spirit to pull the spirit back from the Shadowlands. And it's going to require and extended roll, drown you in paradox and maybe piss off some death-related entity. Let's say there's a reason if there is no record of a proper resurrection in the WOD. =P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T08:28:51-07:00","id":1155735,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1155705#post1155705\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Said pet Mage would need some seriously high Spheres to succeed in this way as only the direct intervention of a Celestine gets to mess about with this (and also it states right after the Tribal Homelands line that no Gift, Discipline or Magic can reconnect an Abominations spirit with the Tribal Homelands short of direct Celestine Intervention, which is crazy high sphere magic).</div> </div> </div> </div>Only celestines can mess with the gnosis role. The mage would only come in after the role was made.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1155726#post1155726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resurrection is bound to be <i>quite </i>hard to pull out (conjunction effect of Spirit, Mind and Life) and probably requiring an Archmaster of Spirit to pull the spirit back from the Shadowlands. And it's going to require and extended roll, drown you in paradox and maybe piss off some death-related entity. Let's say there's a reason if there is no record of a proper resurrection in the WOD. =P</div> </div> </div> </div>Resurrection would really only require life 5(creating new life) spirit 5(effecting a spirit-like entity, the garou soul) if both the body and spirit are present(which would be a given if said garou dies in the presence of a mage with spirit 5). You don't need to create a new mind as the soul will already have one. You'd definitely piss of gaia and her incarnae(who'd likely inform the garou through visions and spirit-quests of what you're doing).<br /> <br /> Paradox would be a non-factor if you're doing this in a sanctum or said vampire's magical lab, their are no non-magic witnesses and you'll be in a reality zone with a heavy &quot;dark/evil/blood magic&quot; resonance so your defilement of the god's creations would even be at reduced difficulty.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T08:50:44-07:00","id":1155741,"title":"","content":"Granted, the only kind of vamp that'd have the knowledge and power to create an abomination factory like that would be an elder wyrm infernalist with a nephandi blood familiar. So the only in meta vamp that could pull off making a demon enthralled abomination-fomori factory would be harold zettler in pentex's special projects division.<br /> <br /> I.E. something that a campaign would be built around to stop.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-04T14:32:16-07:00","id":1155857,"title":"","content":"Minimum Spirit 5, Life 5, Matter 2, Correspondence 3 requiring approx 20 successes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T04:09:06-08:00","id":1155999,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1155857#post1155857\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Minimum Spirit 5, Life 5, Matter 2, Correspondence 3 requiring approx 20 successes.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need matter to effect dead things and It don't understand why you need correspondence. Unless the mage doesn't have the spirit on hand, Then I understand that said mage just let the wolf spirit get away to tell all it's friends and ancestors what happening(I.E. that's one dumb nephendi)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T04:30:50-08:00","id":1156005,"title":"","content":"Given that the spirit goes directly to the Tribal Homelands (unless for some even rarer reason the Werewolf Wraith's) the odds on managing to complete the rote in the moment before the spirit part of the Garou is IN the Tribal homelands are fairly marginal.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T05:34:08-08:00","id":1156019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1156005#post1156005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Given that the spirit goes directly to the Tribal Homelands (unless for some even rarer reason the Werewolf Wraith's) the odds on managing to complete the rote in the moment before the spirit part of the Garou is IN the Tribal homelands are fairly marginal.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a mage with spirit 5 though, they could simply entrap the spirit in an ephimeral cage. Unless you'd rule that the spirit teleports their without ant travel in the umbra.<br /> <br /> I which case the nephandus Would need Correspondence 4 as well as Spirit 5 to create a ban zone/reality bubble the spirit can't teleport out of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T06:04:43-08:00","id":1156024,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1155735#post1155735\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Resurrection would really only require life 5(creating new life) spirit 5(effecting a spirit-like entity, the garou soul) if both the body and spirit are present(which would be a given if said garou dies in the presence of a mage with spirit 5). You don't need to create a new mind as the soul will already have one. You'd definitely piss of gaia and her incarnae(who'd likely inform the garou through visions and spirit-quests of what you're doing).</div> </div> </div> </div>Hrrm, I'm not sure about the lack of Mind magic, I think you may still need to create a mind where the spirit's memory are poured. And yes, the tribal homelands are going to be a pain to breach, you may even have an aspect of the Incarna barring your soul poaching. A spirit cage is probably their best shot, but requires the mage to know how the Garou souls work - and that may require some experiments to figure out, it's not that easy for a mage to realise that the Homelands exist.<br /> <br /> Anyway, those vampires are going to need a quite powerful mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T06:22:46-08:00","id":1156029,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1156024#post1156024\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hrrm, I'm not sure about the lack of Mind magic, I think you may still need to create a mind where the spirit's memory are poured. And yes, the tribal homelands are going to be a pain to breach, you may even have an aspect of the Incarna barring your soul poaching. A spirit cage is probably their best shot, but requires the mage to know how the Garou souls work - and that may require some experiments to figure out, it's not that easy for a mage to realise that the Homelands exist.<br /> <br /> Anyway, those vampires are going to need a quite powerful mage.</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking blood familiars though it's more likely they'll be Itarajana pillar/lokas users, who have Life/(middle umbra)Spirit/Mind as a single pillar(triagyoni, but if you'd require entropy/correspondence to be involved the pillar uta has that covered).<br /> <br /> This would mean the tal'mahe'ra are involved in said abomination factory(which they'd have reason to honestly, they employ abominations as weapons whenever they find one. they're basiclly meaty seige engines that they can point in a given direction and say &quot;that's the guy responsible for turning you into an abomination to gaia&quot; only to sit back and watch the fireworks.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T08:32:16-08:00","id":1156062,"title":"","content":"Not that I think this is particularly helpful, but at this point the &quot;pet Mage&quot; is a master of several Spheres, performing a complex Ritual every to every other day or so. Just admit it's ST fiat and move on.<br /> <br /> While this <i>might</i> technically be possible system-wise, it doesn't seem like it should work out terrible well in-Setting without the story requiring that it work for the Story to work. <br /> <br /> I think you are better of not overly involving Spirit and making the argument that the Mage is saving the Garou with Time just before the moment of death. I think the Sphere requirements would be significantly less and not involve having to be overly familiar with the what happens to Garou souls upon death. You know, since Garou don't even fully understand that concept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T11:59:11-08:00","id":1156109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1156062#post1156062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I think this is particularly helpful, but at this point the &quot;pet Mage&quot; is a master of several Spheres, performing a complex Ritual every to every other day or so. Just admit it's ST fiat and move on.<br /> <br /> While this <i>might</i> technically be possible system-wise, it doesn't seem like it should work out terrible well in-Setting without the story requiring that it work for the Story to work.<br /> <br /> I think you are better of not overly involving Spirit and making the argument that the Mage is saving the Garou with Time just before the moment of death. I think the Sphere requirements would be significantly less and not involve having to be overly familiar with the what happens to Garou souls upon death. You know, since Garou don't even fully understand that concept.</div> </div> </div> </div>Actually... yeah. With m20 time rules that'd only require time 3(reverting to before the round the wolfy made the role). I didn't think of that. If were invoking &quot;all roles will have the same outcome unless the mage changes something&quot; the mage could just have the vampire bite the wolf on the other side of the neck, feed it more/less blood, etc to make small changes to how the embrace happens to change the outcome(make the wolf make a different role).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T18:00:54-08:00","id":1156206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1156062#post1156062\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not that I think this is particularly helpful, but at this point the &quot;pet Mage&quot; is a master of several Spheres, performing a complex Ritual every to every other day or so. Just admit it's ST fiat and move on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yea, this thread went quite Nerdvana in these last two pages. XD<br /> All in all, the point is that blood bonds aren't really something easy for vampires to do on a Garou.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-05T20:08:14-08:00","id":1156227,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1156206#post1156206\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Yea, this thread went quite Nerdvana in these last two pages. XD<br /> All in all, the point is that blood bonds aren't really something easy for vampires to do on a Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>According to WtA. The going assumption seems to be that the blood needs to be swallowed (and possibly kept down) for a bond to form. There are more than a few Vampire books that present the Bond differently. If a taste were all that were necessary (as some books say/imply) then none of these defenses help much. Obviously that runs counter to the entire point of the Vitae-allergy section, so I always just ignore the Vampire books in this instance.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T05:12:04-08:00","id":1156288,"title":"","content":"Given that the rules are identical to the cross over info from Ghouls: Fatal Addiction it's the same from the VTM side as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T05:20:28-08:00","id":1156289,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1156227#post1156227\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> According to WtA. The going assumption seems to be that the blood needs to be swallowed (and possibly kept down) for a bond to form. There are more than a few Vampire books that present the Bond differently. If a taste were all that were necessary (as some books say/imply) then none of these defenses help much. Obviously that runs counter to the entire point of the Vitae-allergy section, so I always just ignore the Vampire books in this instance.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, for the blood bond this idea was left there and nobody touched it:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This isn't even getting into using something like Engaging the Vessel of Transference (these are thaumaturges) or injecting the blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Using Thaumaturgy (or just needles) makes sense in this particular case (more than Time Mages for sure). Blood bond becomes a lot more likely, since being alergic wouldn't help to regurgitate the blood if it's already in your circulatory system. Although I think it would be thematic to allow the alergic Garou to enter Frenzy and ripp the affected part out of his body before the Bond takes effect","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T05:38:22-08:00","id":1156297,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1156289#post1156289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using Thaumaturgy (or just needles) makes sense in this particular case (more than Time Mages for sure). Blood bond becomes a lot more likely, since being alergic wouldn't help to regurgitate the blood if it's already in your circulatory system. Although I think it would be thematic to allow the alergic Garou to enter Frenzy and ripp the affected part out of his body before the Bond takes effect</div> </div> </div> </div> Very thematic, agreed.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T06:47:28-08:00","id":1156326,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1156289#post1156289\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Using Thaumaturgy (or just needles) makes sense in this particular case (more than Time Mages for sure). Blood bond becomes a lot more likely, since being alergic wouldn't help to regurgitate the blood if it's already in your circulatory system. Although I think it would be thematic to allow the alergic Garou to enter Frenzy and rip the affected part out of his body before the Bond takes effect</div> </div> </div> </div>If we're talking an imprisoned werewolf though, the vamp in question is going to have the furry tornado of destruction restrained(likely with silver cuffs and chains) long before they get anywhere near it with a syringe. More to keep the angry wolfy from tearing their face off than any knowledge of said alergy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T07:20:20-08:00","id":1156333,"title":"","content":"Yes, but silver chains are a bad idea, Werewolf in Frenzy it's going to enter Crinos regardless of damage. Silver it's notoriously frail.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T07:26:11-08:00","id":1156336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1156333#post1156333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yes, but silver chains are a bad idea, Werewolf in Frenzy it's going to enter Crinos regardless of damage. Silver it's notoriously frail.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, if it is strong enough silver chain, you could have your werewolf accidentally corrode their hands/other body parts off. Silver burns, remember.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T10:52:26-08:00","id":1156399,"title":"","content":"The problem is unless it's a very special silver chain it's totally not going to hold for more than 1 round.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T12:37:04-08:00","id":1156438,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1156399#post1156399\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The problem is unless it's a very special silver chain it's totally not going to hold for more than 1 round.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if you made it by alloying in significant amounts of stronger metal, it's not going to count as silver at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T13:01:08-08:00","id":1156451,"title":"","content":"Depends on how thick it is and if it's tempered, but it probably wouldn't be the first time a ventrue was pasted by relying on silver too much. Functional titanium or polymer restraint to do the work and add decorative silver chains to weaken the wolfy but not hold anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T14:58:58-08:00","id":1156490,"title":"","content":"Also you ideally don't want the Silver in contact with the Garou's flesh at all (some cloth needs to be between metal and skin/fur) or the Garou will be Raging back from Incap and either tearing free or dying within a few minutes of the chains gong on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-06T15:11:34-08:00","id":1156495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1156490#post1156490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also you ideally don't want the Silver in contact with the Garou's flesh at all (some cloth needs to be between metal and skin/fur) or the Garou will be Raging back from Incap and either tearing free or dying within a few minutes of the chains gong on.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or, like I said above, just outright lobbing the body part off it if is a limb.<br /> <br /> Something like a carved stone bench would be more useful than silver, as silver is like playing with acid with garou.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-07T01:00:11-08:00","id":1156606,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the ideas and input.<br /> <br /> I\u2019ve come to the conclusion that my vampire mages:<br /> <br /> -Have heard rumors of Abominations exist, they have never seen a proof of their existence, but the rumor says it\u2019s very difficult to happen (urban legend). Therefore the Vampires are going to keep the garous alive to experiment.<br /> <br /> -The vampires have never heard of the Garous allergy to the vampire blood. I guess vampires usually don\u2019t survive after realizing the Garou is not blood bonded to them\u2026<br /> <br /> -I\u2019m going to allow the PCs to role for their allergy, so it\u2019s unlikely they\u2019ll get blood bounded. Then depending on how the PCs handle the situation we\u2019ll move on. They can pretend they are friendly to the vampires and slay them after getting over their dominate and presence. Or they can remain aggressive and let the vampires try new things like blood transfers once the vampires realize the Garou pock their blood.<br /> <br /> (No Nephando mages XD )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11010-ersito","name":"erSito","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11010_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"119"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T04:06:53-08:00","id":1157492,"title":"","content":"How about a Silver dome completely physical means of breaking out and spiritual because tis made from silver. That should effect their Gnosis if they still use that rule. You may need cameras, some far fetched means of keeping them fed.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T08:32:26-08:00","id":1157547,"title":"","content":"An angry garou will rip through that in seconds and take maybe a couple of agg levels for their trouble, Or they will use the reflection in silver to step sideways and leave that way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T08:46:58-08:00","id":1158483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Moirdryd</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1157547#post1157547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">An angry garou will rip through that in seconds and take maybe a couple of agg levels for their trouble, Or they will use the reflection in silver to step sideways and leave that way.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> tarnished silver(still works) and you use steel to reinforce the dome itself.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19321-kewlimp","name":"kewlimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T13:05:33-08:00","id":1158605,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kewlimp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1158483#post1158483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> tarnished silver(still works) and you use steel to reinforce the dome itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Composite construction disrupts the spiritual effect that you're going for, probably even if it isn't alloyed, because you intend for a dome to do something, and if it is not completely silver, better luck next time. Also, it feels like you'd need to clean tarnish off of a silver object before the spirit decides to give any more fucks about doing anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T15:51:30-08:00","id":1158678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1158605#post1158605\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Composite construction disrupts the spiritual effect that you're going for, probably even if it isn't alloyed, because you intend for a dome to do something, and if it is not completely silver, better luck next time. Also, it feels like you'd need to clean tarnish off of a silver object before the spirit decides to give any more fucks about doing anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its wouldn't be an alloy by any real means. Maybe I misphrased. Its a second dome on the outside of the first silver dome. To cover the silver thing, I haven't read anywhere that states it must be clean, polished silver. Just silver. I don't remember reading about alloys either but that sounds right and I like to take people's word on things like that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19321-kewlimp","name":"kewlimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-14T18:44:36-08:00","id":1158737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kewlimp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1158678#post1158678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Its wouldn't be an alloy by any real means.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know (in case my own post wasn't clear about that, I did completely understand what you were talking about). Alloying is just one way that you can make spirits upset. Positioning different metals around each other probably doesn't make them happy as far as the construction of the dome as a single thing goes. Also, how would you plan to go about bonding said pieces of the dome together? Because you can't just stick the two things together.<br /> <br /> Lastly, you have to consider that steel reinforcement won't stop the Garou from tearing through it. What is this child of iron but more material for a werewolf to shear and bash through, a wild force of nature that cannot be stopped?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Maybe I misphrased. Its a second dome on the outside of the first silver dome. To cover the silver thing, I haven't read anywhere that states it must be clean, polished silver. Just silver. </div> </div> </div>Tarnish is a layer of a silver compound over silver. This is roughly as effective as silver nitrate or silver chloride at causing aggravated damage to werewolves, which is to say, not at all. It's probably remedied more easily than other chemical processes, since it just involves some quick chemical scrubbing to get it off, but until you do this, it would likely be ineffective.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I don't remember reading about alloys either but that sounds right and I like to take people's word on things like that. </div> </div> </div>There's a discussion of that in W20 where it describes the effects of silver. When you go below 90-ish percent purity, it stops counting as silver by the way spirits judge things.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","user":"Saur Ops Specialist","date":". 11-14-2017, 09:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T00:23:28-08:00","id":1158791,"title":"","content":"Question: is everyone here absolutely sure that silver manacles are going to break under the Garou's transformation?<br /> Because as he changes form his body stops offering any kind of resistance to silver and it still would make sense to me if as the wrists get bigger the handcuffs simply stays where they are, cutting the meat as it grows and biting into the bone. The hands are going to be unusable that way (no tendrils), the damage is not easily regenerable and it's even worse if the chain was tying the neck. That is also not going to free the Garou from whatever thing he's chained to, so by morphing he's basically going to just harm himself.<br /> <br /> Is there any RAW on this thing?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T03:47:48-08:00","id":1158857,"title":"","content":"Though I do not recall if there were any ever rules published BSDs do have a Fetish/Talen silver cuff restraint that inhibits the ability to shift shape. This would suggest that regular silver while painful and dangerous just isn't put the task. Iirc there is also a story in one of the books where the antagonists go &quot;Those restraints are silver so don't even think about shifting&quot; and a few moments later the bound Garou takes some nasty wounds in the process of shifting and ripping himself free. <br /> <br /> Typically the wounds done by silver don't change in type compared to what they'd be if inflicted by a none silver object they're just harder to heal, hurt a ton more and are more catastrophic as the Garou cannot soak them. A silver blade does to Garou flesh what a steel one does to a regular humans, a silver club will break bones and rupture muscles upon a Garou with consummate ease compared to that which a wooden one would break a humans (and that's still nasty in and of itself) but nothing in turn prevents the silver object from suffering damage in its own right (there's a discussion on this in a dark ages book I think in regards to silver weapons) and there's nothing to suggest that the silver gains any additional integrity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-15T07:02:32-08:00","id":1158928,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1158737#post1158737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I know (in case my own post wasn't clear about that, I did completely understand what you were talking about). Alloying is just one way that you can make spirits upset. Positioning different metals around each other probably doesn't make them happy as far as the construction of the dome as a single thing goes. Also, how would you plan to go about bonding said pieces of the dome together? Because you can't just stick the two things together.<br /> <br /> Lastly, you have to consider that steel reinforcement won't stop the Garou from tearing through it. What is this child of iron but more material for a werewolf to shear and bash through, a wild force of nature that cannot be stopped?</div> </div> </div> </div>For this part. It doesn't have to be bonded together. Making up numbers here, a 9 foot cage of silver and outside that a 9 foot and an inch steel cage. The steel is a buffing, in crinos, its flesh will be pressed up against a lot of silver. Now Rips Your Faceoff has to make a choice: take the damage while ripping through the steel or find another way out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Tarnish is a layer of a silver compound over silver. This is roughly as effective as silver nitrate or silver chloride at causing aggravated damage to werewolves, which is to say, not at all. It's probably remedied more easily than other chemical processes, since it just involves some quick chemical scrubbing to get it off, but until you do this, it would likely be ineffective.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> There's a discussion of that in W20 where it describes the effects of silver. When you go below 90-ish percent purity, it stops counting as silver by the way spirits judge things. </div> </div> </div>Maybe tarnished isn't the right word. What I meant by tarnished is unpolished, I forget if I clarified that. Its still pure silver, its just not reflective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19321-kewlimp","name":"kewlimp","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"36"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T10:38:10-08:00","id":1159910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1158737#post1158737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know (in case my own post wasn't clear about that, I did completely understand what you were talking about). Alloying is just one way that you can make spirits upset. Positioning different metals around each other probably doesn't make them happy as far as the construction of the dome as a single thing goes. Also, how would you plan to go about bonding said pieces of the dome together? Because you can't just stick the two things together.<br /> <br /> Lastly, you have to consider that steel reinforcement won't stop the Garou from tearing through it. What is this child of iron but more material for a werewolf to shear and bash through, a wild force of nature that cannot be stopped?</div> </div> </div> </div>You are really over-estimating how strong garou are. By the strength charts provided by W20(p 270-271), you'd need strength 11 to rip open a 1&quot; steel sheet(and if it's thicker you're boned, going from a steel drum of 0.0324&quot; to 1&quot; is 1 strength. Therefore I'd rule every additional inch requires 1 more dot) which, unless you have superhuman strength Before adding on crinos or a gift that increases strength on a character with world class strength, is impossible.<br /> <br /> Considering a bank vault is at least 1 foot of steel(rebar network of up to 4&quot; of thickness) and concrete, and the fact that said vault's aren't build with the worry the money will try to break Out(which whatever a vampire makes to hold a garou Will) I'd say the graou is Not breaking out.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>kewlimp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1158928#post1158928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> For this part. It doesn't have to be bonded together. Making up numbers here, a 9 foot cage of silver and outside that a 9 foot and an inch steel cage. The steel is a buffing, in crinos, its flesh will be pressed up against a lot of silver. Now Rips Your Faceoff has to make a choice: take the damage while ripping through the steel or find another way out.<br /> <br /> Maybe tarnished isn't the right word. What I meant by tarnished is unpolished, I forget if I clarified that. Its still pure silver, its just not reflective.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could simply have a rough surface so that light is scattered rather than reflected.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T12:24:46-08:00","id":1159966,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1159910#post1159910\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could simply have a rough surface so that light is scattered rather than reflected.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wouldn't putting off the lights be enough?, no light, no reflection.<br /> <br /> Anycase, I like this idea better than the chains...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> You are really over-estimating how strong garou are. By the strength charts provided by W20(p 270-271), you'd need strength 11 to rip open a 1&quot; steel sheet(and if it's thicker you're boned, going from a steel drum of 0.0324&quot; to 1&quot; is 1 strength. Therefore I'd rule every additional inch requires 1 more dot) which, unless you have superhuman strength Before adding on crinos or a gift that increases strength on a character with world class strength, is impossible. </div> </div> </div>Technically, you can roll Willpower at diff 8 for a few more &quot;points&quot; if you use that table. But I agree in that it would be very resistent unless the Garou has Gifts (far from rare, but not always present)...The silver dome it's more sound that the silver chain, albeit it still has one problem:<br /> <br /> You have to take in count that a hit with the claws that wouldn't be enough to rip steel, may be more than enough to rip the silver plate-leaving only the steel plate that doesn't cause aggravated. I think you may need a very deep silver plate to cause more than one or two Aggravated this way.<br /> <br /> Also, I would hesitate to put in a jail something the prisoner can use to suicide, since my intent it's to keep it alive to do nasty Thaumaturgic experiments.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T13:09:03-08:00","id":1159986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1159966#post1159966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't putting off the lights be enough?, no light, no reflection.<br /> <br /> Anycase, I like this idea better than the chains...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Technically, you can roll Willpower at diff 8 for a few more &quot;points&quot; if you use that table. But I agree in that it would be very resistent unless the Garou has Gifts (far from rare, but not always present)...The silver dome it's more sound that the silver chain, albeit it still has one problem:<br /> <br /> You have to take in count that a hit with the claws that wouldn't be enough to rip steel, may be more than enough to rip the silver plate-leaving only the steel plate that doesn't cause aggravated. I think you may need a very deep silver plate to cause more than one or two Aggravated this way.<br /> <br /> Also, I would hesitate to put in a jail something the prisoner can use to suicide, since my intent it's to keep it alive to do nasty Thaumaturgic experiments.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Bone Gnawers even have a first-ranked Gift to make feats of strength easier, albeit at the cost of voluntary bashing damage. Higher-ranked characters might not even need to bother, and certain scar fetishes or other concealable spirit-binding tricks might simply cut through the Gordian Knot of the dome through other means, such as a slagger talen (consult the older Glass Walkers tribe book) melting part of it open, or being a child of the Monkey King totem, which reduces the difficulty of all rolls to escape or evade captivity by 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-17T22:40:29-08:00","id":1160130,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1159966#post1159966\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Wouldn't putting off the lights be enough?, no light, no reflection.<br /> <br /> Anycase, I like this idea better than the chains...<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Technically, you can roll Willpower at diff 8 for a few more &quot;points&quot; if you use that table. But I agree in that it would be very resistent unless the Garou has Gifts (far from rare, but not always present)...The silver dome it's more sound that the silver chain, albeit it still has one problem:<br /> <br /> You have to take in count that a hit with the claws that wouldn't be enough to rip steel, may be more than enough to rip the silver plate-leaving only the steel plate that doesn't cause aggravated. I think you may need a very deep silver plate to cause more than one or two Aggravated this way.<br /> <br /> Also, I would hesitate to put in a jail something the prisoner can use to suicide, since my intent it's to keep it alive to do nasty Thaumaturgic experiments.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I thought the wp role was diff 9?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1159986#post1159986\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Bone Gnawers even have a first-ranked Gift to make feats of strength easier, albeit at the cost of voluntary bashing damage. Higher-ranked characters might not even need to bother, and certain scar fetishes or other concealable spirit-binding tricks might simply cut through the Gordian Knot of the dome through other means, such as a slagger talen (consult the older Glass Walkers tribe book) melting part of it open, or being a child of the Monkey King totem, which reduces the difficulty of all rolls to escape or evade captivity by 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it would really depend on how well fortified the dome was. Said garou with monkey totem and desperate strength will still be capped at +5 strength from the Feat role bringing at strength 5 character in crinos to a wopping 14. Unless the Vampires were super prepared(or had a bank vault, 4&quot; steel rebar and 8&quot; of concrete is to much for anything less than 15 in my book.which unless you're a rank 6 phillidox/galliard with &quot;break the bonds&quot; isn't happening) the bone gnawer garou has a good chance of escape, probably a good reason they and glass walkers(slagger talen) are the ones who can handle living in cities.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T15:32:40-08:00","id":1160338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1160130#post1160130\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I thought the wp role was diff 9?</div> </div> </div> </div>It varies depending on what you're trying to do. The set difficulty of 9 is pre-W20.<br /> <br /> [quote-<br /> Yeah, it would really depend on how well fortified the dome was. Said garou with monkey totem and desperate strength will still be capped at +5 strength from the Feat role bringing at strength 5 character in crinos to a wopping 14. Unless the Vampires were super prepared(or had a bank vault, 4&quot; steel rebar and 8&quot; of concrete is to much for anything less than 15 in my book.which unless you're a rank 6 phillidox/galliard with &quot;break the bonds&quot; isn't happening) the bone gnawer garou has a good chance of escape, probably a good reason they and glass walkers(slagger talen) are the ones who can handle living in cities.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I don't actually think that ease of escape is the reason why they can better handle living in cities. It can be useful and important, but it's not the main reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-18T19:21:06-08:00","id":1160388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1160338#post1160338\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It varies depending on what you're trying to do. The set difficulty of 9 is pre-W20.<br /> <br /> I don't actually think that ease of escape is the reason why they can better handle living in cities. It can be useful and important, but it's not the main reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>it's also the W20 standard given on the same page they go over feats of strength.<br /> <br /> For point 2 was a bit of a joke, though I do think that If you're playing &quot;one world of Darkness&quot; Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers are going to run into A Lot more Vamps(even with a 1/100,000 to 1/1001 ratio[varying by ST] the Ironfisted control vampires hold over the major cities in VTM will come up more than the wyrm leeches in WTA).<br /> <br /> I personally Like to Use the Technocracy as a major Tie for why humanity would stomp vampires if they revealed themselves and why the weaver is winning as completely as it is(On Earth, Wolfies and the Traditions own the spirit world, with changelings and wraiths owning the higher and lower penumbras respectively).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-19T09:32:56-08:00","id":1160535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1160388#post1160388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> it's also the W20 standard given on the same page they go over feats of strength.</div> </div> </div> </div>The flex on difficulty is an important addition, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For point 2 was a bit of a joke, though I do think that If you're playing &quot;one world of Darkness&quot; Bone Gnawers and Glass Walkers are going to run into A Lot more Vamps(even with a 1/100,000 to 1/1001 ratio[varying by ST] the Ironfisted control vampires hold over the major cities in VTM will come up more than the wyrm leeches in WTA). </div> </div> </div>Glass Walkers and Bone Gnawers tend to buy more WP at chargen to avoid exploding at all the irritations of the city all the time. As it turns out, it also helps here!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I personally Like to Use the Technocracy as a major Tie for why humanity would stomp vampires if they revealed themselves and why the weaver is winning as completely as it is(On Earth, Wolfies and the Traditions own the spirit world, with changelings and wraiths owning the higher and lower penumbras respectively). </div> </div> </div>Mage has too much baggage on setting definitions to be a good tie-in for anything but Mage. Also, the Dreaming is different from the Astral Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-20T06:14:39-08:00","id":1160831,"title":"","content":"Don't forget also that the Feats of Strength chart isn't just always Strength stat but depending on what you're trying to achieve can be Strength + Athletics or even Melee and that steel dome is only as strong as it's rivets and an average Strength Garou with Average Athletics is going to rip that dome open with 1 success on that WP roll and spending a point of Willpower. Add in anything past average and it's easier, throw in some Ancestors background maybe or a Gift or some Totem bonus and the werewolf is leaving.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2767-moirdryd","name":"Moirdryd","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2767_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"490"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T13:36:29-08:00","id":1161260,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1160535#post1160535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mage has too much baggage on setting definitions to be a good tie-in for anything but Mage. Also, the Dreaming is different from the Astral Umbra.</div> </div> </div> </div>CWOD books all subscribe to the &quot;Unreliable Narrator&quot; trope anyway, so when the subject comes up al that happens is an in character arguement over their perspective on how something works and when it doesn't it doesn't matter.<br /> <br /> As for the astral-Dreaming thing, I'm not entirely an expert on spiritual physics, but I'm pretty sure two dimensions can occupy the same &quot;location&quot; in the weird cosmos that we see. The dreaming itself is definitely high umbral in how I interpret it(it's the litteral nexus of dreams after all) and it has layers as close to reality as the penumbra, therefore I put it them there. You can interpret things differently and that's fine. the books Have given a definite answer on where the astral plane is in the spirit world, and Haven't for the dreaming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T16:52:57-08:00","id":1161337,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1161260#post1161260\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> CWOD books all subscribe to the &quot;Unreliable Narrator&quot; trope anyway, so when the subject comes up al that happens is an in character arguement over their perspective on how something works and when it doesn't it doesn't matter.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. They do not. Not for everything, and Werewolf the least of all, since a number of uncertainties are juggled and never broached again as anything worth mentioning. Gaia maybe not being the entirety of existence? Ancestor-spirits not being actual ancestors? Raised in a sentence or two when introduced, and never heard from again while the game goes in a distinct direction away from them at top speed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for the astral-Dreaming thing, I'm not entirely an expert on spiritual physics, but I'm pretty sure two dimensions can occupy the same &quot;location&quot; in the weird cosmos that we see. The dreaming itself is definitely high umbral in how I interpret it(it's the litteral nexus of dreams after all) and it has layers as close to reality as the penumbra, therefore I put it them there. You can interpret things differently and that's fine. the books Have given a definite answer on where the astral plane is in the spirit world, and Haven't for the dreaming. </div> </div> </div>The Dreaming isn't even Umbral in the slightest, else connections between the Dreaming and the Umbra wouldn't be a thing brought up as weird in books like W20 Umbra. The Dreaming and the Astral could be related, but tying the two together very closely doesn't really do much for Changeling, much less any other game utilizing the Umbra, so it's probably best to not do that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-21T20:20:15-08:00","id":1161403,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1161337#post1161337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. They do not. Not for everything, and Werewolf the least of all, since a number of uncertainties are juggled and never broached again as anything worth mentioning. Gaia maybe not being the entirety of existence? Ancestor-spirits not being actual ancestors? Raised in a sentence or two when introduced, and never heard from again while the game goes in a distinct direction away from them at top speed.</div> </div> </div> </div>As Far as I know the previous books wrote from the perspective of someone in world, W20 may change it up by writing from the perspective of the real world author, but it still assumes the WTA perspective is fact(which is fine for a WTA game, but worrying in a one world perspective, yes)<br /> <br /> There Are however problems with how werewolves view the universe even in a WTA only setting.<br /> <br /> Take Gaia's place in the universe for instance, the garou/authorstry to push the gaia is the world/ all life bearing worlds and their for above the triat and all spirits. That's fine until you consider anything beyond earth's atmosphere, where the sun in the material plane is a cosmic engine of untold chaos and creation that dwarfs the earth the way we dwarf dust-mites, yet is some-how a subservient being to our earth(If gaia is earth). Or how the traitic supernals, the beings who are supposed to represent chaos, order, and entropy respectively all serve gaia(If gaia is all Life).<br /> <br /> The wyld who cosmicly control the unpredictably reactions of minute particles and energies in quantum mechanics, the dance of cosmic rays racing across distances light years wide, the churning matter forges of stars, and who's war-cry forged energy into matter in such intensity it still shakes the universe. The Weaver who takes the dust to forge planets and stars, who leads them into carefully balanced orbits that turn like clockwork, and structures galaxies into delicate spirals. The wyrm who slowly eats at the life of every atom as they lose their charge, who swallows dying stars from within in violent roars, and who's many black eyes devour systems and galaxies beyond the scope of comprehension. All these cosmic forces somehow serve a goddess of &quot;Life&quot;, a concept so rare and insignificant it isn't even detectable on the cosmic scale, and who isn't even refered to as a Supernal in some books, but as a Celestial. I Hardly believe that.<br /> <br /> I honestly think the Werewolf cosmology is their perspective of a spiritual too vast for them to understand, where their &quot;incarnae&quot; are in fact minor gods that have nothing to do with the cosmic order outside of earth's borders and are in fact the spirits of earthly interpretation of those concepts. Helios is not the Star the dwarfs earth, it is the sun as seen from earth. The WTA wyrm is not the engine of cosmic entropy of limitless might, it is but a minute fragment of the cosmic wyrm(if even that) that represents the things the planet is doing to destroy itself.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1161337#post1161337\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Dreaming isn't even Umbral in the slightest, else connections between the Dreaming and the Umbra wouldn't be a thing brought up as weird in books like W20 Umbra. The Dreaming and the Astral could be related, but tying the two together very closely doesn't really do much for Changeling, much less any other game utilizing the Umbra, so it's probably best to not do that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I wasn't saying they were the same thing or even connected, the dreaming and the astral plane can both be planes where the high umbra overlaps earth, but still have nothing to do with each other. The digital web isn't malpheas after all, yet both can connect to, overlap with and interact with the different parts of the middle umbra. Honestly I'm not sure what to do with the dreaming if it isn't connected to the high umbra in any way, It'd be the only cosmology that doesn't interact with the umbra and would become somewhat redundant to have a high umbral dream plane and the dreaming. Not to mention in Dark ages: Fae The Fae themselves come from sprites, Which Are spirits with charms, gnosis and rage, though I honestly don't know how dark ages fae later become modern changelings.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T11:11:40-08:00","id":1161560,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">I wasn't saying they were the same thing or even connected, the dreaming and the astral plane can both be planes where the high umbra overlaps earth, but still have nothing to do with each other. The digital web isn't malpheas after all, yet both can connect to, overlap with and interact with the different parts of the middle umbra. Honestly I'm not sure what to do with the dreaming if it isn't connected to the high umbra in any way, It'd be the only cosmology that doesn't interact with the umbra and would become somewhat redundant to have a high umbral dream plane and the dreaming. Not to mention in Dark ages: Fae The Fae themselves come from sprites, Which Are spirits with charms, gnosis and rage, though I honestly don't know how dark ages fae later become modern changelings.</span></span><br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>The Astral Umbra IT'S the High Umbra. At least in Mage. I think Werewolves use Astral for Mage's Horizon (which isn't in the High Umbra), but I'm not sure.<br /> <br /> \u200bIf you don't want to have the Dreaming as something separate from the Umbra your best bet it's to rewind time to the era of the Book of Worlds and fusion it with the Dream Zone. There's no need to have two places dedicated to dreams and fantasy. Also Zones can overlap with all of the Umbra and may not respect Umbral laws or boundaries, so it's not as restrictive as it may seem.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Take Gaia's place in the universe for instance, the garou/authorstry to push the gaia is the world/ all life bearing worlds and their for above the triat and all spirits. That's fine until you consider anything beyond earth's atmosphere, where the sun in the material plane is a cosmic engine of untold chaos and creation that dwarfs the earth the way we dwarf dust-mites, yet is some-how a subservient being to our earth(If gaia is earth). Or how the traitic supernals, the beings who are supposed to represent chaos, order, and entropy respectively all serve gaia(If gaia is all Life).<br /> <br /> The wyld who cosmicly control the unpredictably reactions of minute particles and energies in quantum mechanics, the dance of cosmic rays racing across distances light years wide, the churning matter forges of stars, and who's war-cry forged energy into matter in such intensity it still shakes the universe. The Weaver who takes the dust to forge planets and stars, who leads them into carefully balanced orbits that turn like clockwork, and structures galaxies into delicate spirals. The wyrm who slowly eats at the life of every atom as they lose their charge, who swallows dying stars from within in violent roars, and who's many black eyes devour systems and galaxies beyond the scope of comprehension. All these cosmic forces somehow serve a goddess of &quot;Life&quot;, a concept so rare and insignificant it isn't even detectable on the cosmic scale, and who isn't even refered to as a Supernal in some books, but as a Celestial. I Hardly believe that.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's worth to note that from the point of view of an animist metaphysic, everithing it's alive. The &quot;anima&quot; it's literaly what defines &quot;Life&quot;, and thus Gaia purview would encompass all spirits from the humble human soul to the real-world Sun itself. Possibly even the Triat. &quot;Lifeless&quot; planets, stars, and particles would be alive, and perhaps even conscious in an animistic world, and thus part of Gaia.<br /> This ties to the concept of &quot;all the spirits are one&quot;, that exist in Werewolf and, to a lesser extent, in Mage (Dreamspeakers)-in Werewolf it's the place of &quot;the Gaia that Was&quot;, which it's not Earth.<br /> By using the scientific concept of &quot;Life&quot; you are muddling the metaphysics.<br /> <br /> Also Supernal it's an interesting word . I think they weren't really mentioned outside Exalted-Which it's no longer the past of WoD. Again, you're muddling the waters with a concept that doesn't exit in Werewolf<br /> <br /> It seems to me that these &quot;problems&quot; have little to do with &quot;how werewolves view the universe in a WTA only setting&quot; and a lot to do with your own understanding of how WoD should work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 11-22-2017, 02:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-22T12:50:43-08:00","id":1161588,"title":"","content":"As of W20, the High Umbra is the same for Werewolf and Mage. Horizon is a thing that doesn't matter in Werewolf and so is never really discussed beyond a very brief mention in Umbra Revised; it's presumably there, but not something that Garou or Fera interact with to any degree of regularity.<br /> <br /> (It was different in prior editions, where what Mage called the High Umbra, Werewolf called the Deep Umbra, and what Mage called the Deep Umbra, Werewolf knew as the quite physical expanse of space beyond Earth.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1161403#post1161403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As Far as I know the previous books wrote from the perspective of someone in world, W20 may change it up by writing from the perspective of the real world author, but it still assumes the WTA perspective is fact(which is fine for a WTA game, but worrying in a one world perspective, yes)<br /> <br /> There Are however problems with how werewolves view the universe even in a WTA only setting.<br /> <br /> Take Gaia's place in the universe for instance, the garou/authorstry to push the gaia is the world/ all life bearing worlds and their for above the triat and all spirits. That's fine until you consider anything beyond earth's atmosphere, where the sun in the material plane is a cosmic engine of untold chaos and creation that dwarfs the earth the way we dwarf dust-mites, yet is some-how a subservient being to our earth(If gaia is earth). Or how the traitic supernals, the beings who are supposed to represent chaos, order, and entropy respectively all serve gaia(If gaia is all Life).<br /> <br /> The wyld who cosmicly control the unpredictably reactions of minute particles and energies in quantum mechanics, the dance of cosmic rays racing across distances light years wide, the churning matter forges of stars, and who's war-cry forged energy into matter in such intensity it still shakes the universe. The Weaver who takes the dust to forge planets and stars, who leads them into carefully balanced orbits that turn like clockwork, and structures galaxies into delicate spirals. The wyrm who slowly eats at the life of every atom as they lose their charge, who swallows dying stars from within in violent roars, and who's many black eyes devour systems and galaxies beyond the scope of comprehension. All these cosmic forces somehow serve a goddess of &quot;Life&quot;, a concept so rare and insignificant it isn't even detectable on the cosmic scale, and who isn't even refered to as a Supernal in some books, but as a Celestial. I Hardly believe that.<br /> <br /> I honestly think the Werewolf cosmology is their perspective of a spiritual too vast for them to understand, where their &quot;incarnae&quot; are in fact minor gods that have nothing to do with the cosmic order outside of earth's borders and are in fact the spirits of earthly interpretation of those concepts. Helios is not the Star the dwarfs earth, it is the sun as seen from earth. The WTA wyrm is not the engine of cosmic entropy of limitless might, it is but a minute fragment of the cosmic wyrm(if even that) that represents the things the planet is doing to destroy itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you want to completely shit on Werewolf, I suppose you could assume that, but the Garou and Fera have swept far around, because traveling through the Aetherial Realm is easy compared to putting rockets together, and you can even step sideways to end up physically on another planet, an asteroid, a large moon, etc. Just make sure that you have Adaptation, Survivor or the like, or you're going to die before you can step back into the Penumbra. The limits of sight from the physical vantage point of where they live on Earth are not something that enters into matters of spirits.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wasn't saying they were the same thing or even connected, the dreaming and the astral plane can both be planes where the high umbra overlaps earth, but still have nothing to do with each other. The digital web isn't malpheas after all, yet both can connect to, overlap with and interact with the different parts of the middle umbra. Honestly I'm not sure what to do with the dreaming if it isn't connected to the high umbra in any way, It'd be the only cosmology that doesn't interact with the umbra and would become somewhat redundant to have a high umbral dream plane and the dreaming. Not to mention in Dark ages: Fae The Fae themselves come from sprites, Which Are spirits with charms, gnosis and rage, though I honestly don't know how dark ages fae later become modern changelings. </div> </div> </div>It's primarily connected to the Middle Umbra when it's connected to any part of it at all. Also, part of the process of becoming Changeling is covered in the recent DA crossover book, with other bits in C20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T21:30:30-08:00","id":1162085,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1161560#post1161560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's worth to note that from the point of view of an animist metaphysic, everithing it's alive. The &quot;anima&quot; it's literaly what defines &quot;Life&quot;, and thus Gaia purview would encompass all spirits from the humble human soul to the real-world Sun itself. Possibly even the Triat. &quot;Lifeless&quot; planets, stars, and particles would be alive, and perhaps even conscious in an animistic world, and thus part of Gaia.<br /> This ties to the concept of &quot;all the spirits are one&quot;, that exist in Werewolf and, to a lesser extent, in Mage (Dreamspeakers)-in Werewolf it's the place of &quot;the Gaia that Was&quot;, which it's not Earth.<br /> By using the scientific concept of &quot;Life&quot; you are muddling the metaphysics.<br /> <br /> Also Supernal it's an interesting word . I think they weren't really mentioned outside Exalted-Which it's no longer the past of WoD. Again, you're muddling the waters with a concept that doesn't exit in Werewolf<br /> <br /> It seems to me that these &quot;problems&quot; have little to do with &quot;how werewolves view the universe in a WTA only setting&quot; and a lot to do with your own understanding of how WoD should work.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1161588#post1161588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to completely shit on Werewolf, I suppose you could assume that, but the Garou and Fera have swept far around, because traveling through the Aetherial Realm is easy compared to putting rockets together, and you can even step sideways to end up physically on another planet, an asteroid, a large moon, etc. Just make sure that you have Adaptation, Survivor or the like, or you're going to die before you can step back into the Penumbra. The limits of sight from the physical vantage point of where they live on Earth are not something that enters into matters of spirits.<br /> in C20.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Have to admit, Werewolf metaphysics(and mage even more so) confuse me. WOD comes with the caveat &quot;it's our world, but&quot; and real Physics are supposedly accepted, but some things just don't align to me. Having gaia being the lord of spirits because all spirits are &quot;Alive&quot; in a sense kinda works, but I then don't get how earth is important in any way or why &quot;gaia is dieing as it does&quot;(it's a tiny wet dust particle in the grand scheme of things).<br /> <br /> If we except there's a wider universe and A.) gaia is the universal spirit-god then earth should have no bearing on gaia's well being and matter little to any but the incarnae of earth's natural world. If we except the wider universe and B.) accept that gaia is damaged/dieing to any significant degree do to the damage to earth's nature, then gaia Cannot be a universal god. If we Don't accept that there is a wider universe, then like mage all realism is lost and we're just pretending it's still there.<br /> <br /> While this might not matter in-game per-say, I personally am to steeped in the understanding of science to simply accept that there are no real physics. The existence of magic, I can fully except, the world if full of things we do not yet understand and the scientific method is designed off of excepting the fact we don't know everything. On the other hand, with all the repeated research and experimentation that has brought forth and proven our understanding of the universe thus far(as small as it might be) that has also supposedly been done in WOD as well, accepting that it's wrong is a much more difficult pill to swallow and it becomes much easier to reason that the faction of homicidally angry tribalists(that once thought murdering the only group of fera maintaining their steady birth rate(apis), the fera that kept gaia's cairns clean(grondr), and attempted the same with their ownly friendly healers(gurahl) in the war of rage was a great plan) don't completely understand the universe the way they think they do(yes I see the irony, but I stand by my point)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T22:07:50-08:00","id":1162095,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1162085#post1162085\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I Have to admit, Werewolf metaphysics(and mage even more so) confuse me. WOD comes with the caveat &quot;it's our world, but&quot; and real Physics are supposedly accepted, but some things just don't align to me. Having gaia being the lord of spirits because all spirits are &quot;Alive&quot; in a sense kinda works, but I then don't get how earth is important in any way or why &quot;gaia is dieing as it does&quot;(it's a tiny wet dust particle in the grand scheme of things).</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's approach it metatextually - Werewolf was created in what seems to be significant part because of outrage at destruction and degradation of the world. One would therefore expect it to concentrate on this planet here that we we live on as the most important part of the setting. Which it does, because no one's going to other planets and no one's finding places to actually escape the dissolution. You stay and fight, because anything else is self-betrayal, and you at least have a chance. Run, and you'll either get eaten, or live to see everything frozen in place, unchanging, as it fades from complete spiritual disconnection. Perhaps even both.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If we except there's a wider universe and A.) gaia is the universal spirit-god then earth should have no bearing on gaia's well being and matter little to any but the incarnae of earth's natural world. If we except the wider universe and B.) accept that gaia is damaged/dieing to any significant degree do to the damage to earth's nature, then gaia Cannot be a universal god. If we Don't accept that there is a wider universe, then like mage all realism is lost and we're just pretending it's still there. </div> </div> </div>Or the existence of life on Earth isn't insignificant, and makes the Earth important accordingly. Mage doesn't enter into it, and what it has to say doesn't matter for anything having to do with Werewolf. Werewolf is about getting angry about having everything taken from you and riding the anger toward change and solving the problems that caused it (ideally). Esoteric field trips to realms that may or may not be divine and holding prisons in deep space that keep Harry, Ron, and Hermione in maximum lockup don't really play well with this setting assumption, so one can assume that they aren't a thing if you're playing Werewolf.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While this might not matter in-game per-say, I personally am to steeped in the understanding of science to simply accept that there are no real physics. The existence of magic, I can fully except, the world if full of things we do not yet understand and the scientific method is designed off of excepting the fact we don't know everything. On the other hand, with all the repeated research and experimentation that has brought forth and proven our understanding of the universe thus far(as small as it might be) that has also supposedly been done in WOD as well, accepting that it's wrong is a much more difficult pill to swallow and it becomes much easier to reason that the faction of homicidally angry tribalists(that once thought murdering the only group of fera maintaining their steady birth rate(apis), the fera that kept gaia's cairns clean(grondr), and attempted the same with their ownly friendly healers(gurahl) in the war of rage was a great plan) don't completely understand the universe the way they think they do(yes I see the irony, but I stand by my point) </div> </div> </div>You can have an intense and far-reaching understanding and still be brought lower than you imagined because of hubris. This is why the world is in the situation it is in, as presented in the text of the game, and metatextually speaking, because the creators presumably didn't want the players handed completely blameless characters with no personal ties to the sordid business of the ages.<br /> <br /> Also, the game isn't too fond of handing out cosmic slaps on the wrist, per the essay in the 2nd edition player's guide. The consequences are more punishment than any deity could ever hope to hand out for the Wars of Rage and other rampages of the past. It would also be terribly counter-productive, given that the main chance for solving the problem without more drastic methods by more powerful beings that might cause even worse problems is for the Garou to get their act together and humble themselves by not exalting the deeds of their ancestors quite so much, particularly where the atrocities that wounded the chances of existence continuing occurred. They have everything else they need but said humility; they are not &quot;primitive&quot; or behind the times; they are acutely aware of what surrounds them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T22:09:51-08:00","id":1162096,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1161588#post1161588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's primarily connected to the Middle Umbra when it's connected to any part of it at all. Also, part of the process of becoming Changeling is covered in the recent DA crossover book, with other bits in C20.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, I always thought that if anything, the order of reason would be responsible for the destruction of the old fae, but apparently managed to do it too themselves. They're a lot like the werewolves in that respect(also means that the reason that most of the supernaturals in WOD can only really blame themselves for where they stand in the modern day. Save apparently the vampires, who honestly where torched to ribbons by humanity and who later also seem to have adjusted better as a whole than most groups.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-23T23:44:14-08:00","id":1162106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1153090-how-a-vampire-would-imprison-a-werewolf?p=1162096#post1162096\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, I always thought that if anything, the order of reason would be responsible 